From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 17:45:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] stm32-stgen: don't panic on resume-time RTC read failure

stm32_stgen_pm_resume() panics if it can't read the RTC calendar, used
only to compensate the STGEN counter for time spent in suspend - not
essential to actually resuming. Same category as the suspend-side fix
(previous commit); this closes the matching gap on resume, confirmed
present in the pristine OP-TEE source (core/drivers/counter/stm32_stgen.c,
extracted from ST's vendor patch) before this branch existed - no prior
patch touched the resume path.

Reviewer note: on a failed read the counter just keeps running from
where it was suspended (slightly behind real time) instead of crashing
resume - no behavior change once the RTC clock-mux fix (see the DT
commit in meta-cargt-stm32mp-addons) makes reads reliable; this is the
fallback for if a read ever isn't.

Signed-off-by: Graham Taylor-Jones <graham.taylor-jones@cargt.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 core/drivers/counter/stm32_stgen.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/core/drivers/counter/stm32_stgen.c b/core/drivers/counter/stm32_stgen.c
index b277106..bef245f 100644
--- a/core/drivers/counter/stm32_stgen.c
+++ b/core/drivers/counter/stm32_stgen.c
@@ -135,16 +135,24 @@ static void stm32_stgen_pm_resume(void)
 	/* STGEN clocks are already restored by the clock driver */
 	io_clrbits32(stgen_d.base + STGENC_CNTCR, BIT(0));

-	/* Read the current time from the RTC to update system counter */
-	if (stm32_rtc_get_calendar(&cur_calendar))
-		panic("Could not get RTC calendar at resume");
-
-	nb_pm_count_ticks = stm32_rtc_diff_calendar_tick(&cur_calendar,
-							 stgen_d.calendar,
-							 clock_src_rate);
-
-	DMSG("Time spent in low-power: %ld ms",
-	     (nb_pm_count_ticks * 1000U) / clock_src_rate);
+	/*
+	 * Don't let a failure here panic resume: this RTC read is only
+	 * used to compensate the STGEN counter for time spent in suspend,
+	 * not essential to actually resuming. Worst case on a failed
+	 * read, skip the drift-compensation update below and leave the
+	 * counter running from where it was suspended (slightly behind
+	 * real time) instead of crashing resume.
+	 */
+	if (stm32_rtc_get_calendar(&cur_calendar)) {
+		EMSG("Could not get RTC calendar at resume, continuing anyway");
+	} else {
+		nb_pm_count_ticks = stm32_rtc_diff_calendar_tick(&cur_calendar,
+								 stgen_d.calendar,
+								 clock_src_rate);
+
+		DMSG("Time spent in low-power: %ld ms",
+		     (nb_pm_count_ticks * 1000U) / clock_src_rate);
+	}

 	/* Update the counter value with the number of pm ticks */
 	if (ADD_OVERFLOW(counter_val, nb_pm_count_ticks, &counter_val))
--
2.43.0
